    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, but isn't it a bit of a stretch to say humanitarian paths are \"more stable\" when so many people are worried about the actual strain on infrastructure, schools, and public services that happens when there isn't strict enforcement? It feels like the enforcement side is being treated as just a \"short-term\" fix instead of a fundamental requirement for a functioning state.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
