      "content": "It is correct that managing infrastructure strain is a critical challenge regardless of the chosen immigration path. However, a system that legally integrates migrants through defined pathways allows for better resource planning and infrastructure scaling than one reliant on uncontrolled influx. Strict enforcement alone often merely displaces issues rather than solving the underlying demographic or labor needs, which integration directly addresses.",
      "source": "target",
